# ============================================================================
# SimePark — environment variables (EXAMPLE FILE, placeholders only)
# ============================================================================
# Copy to `.env` for local development:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` and every `.env.*` file are git-ignored. Only this example file is
# committed, and it must never contain a real value.
#
# TWO SEPARATE GROUPS BELOW. Read which is which before filling anything in.
# ============================================================================


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GROUP 1 — PUBLIC browser configuration (safe to expose, prefixed VITE_)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the JavaScript bundle that is
# served to every visitor. Anything here is PUBLIC. Never put a secret here.

# Your Supabase project URL. Found in: Supabase dashboard > Project Settings >
# Data API > Project URL. Example shape: https://abcdefgh.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Your Supabase PUBLISHABLE key (older projects: the "anon" key). Found in:
# Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API keys.
#
# This key is DESIGNED to be public. It only identifies the project; Row Level
# Security is what actually protects the data. It is safe in the browser.
#
# NEVER put a secret key or a legacy `service_role` key here. Those bypass Row
# Level Security completely. The app detects that mistake and refuses to use the
# key, but do not rely on that check.
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your_supabase_publishable_key_here


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GROUP 2 — SERVER-ONLY secrets (never prefixed with VITE_)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are read ONLY by server code:
#   functions/api/assistant.ts          Cloudflare Pages Function (production)
#   shared/server/handler.ts            the shared handler
#   server/assistantDevMiddleware.ts    local Vite dev middleware
#
# Locally, put them in `.env` (loaded by the dev middleware).
# On Cloudflare they must be configured as encrypted Secrets in the Pages
# project. See the README section "Cloudflare deployment".

# Google AI Studio API key for the AI assistant. Create one at:
#   https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# The assistant is OPTIONAL. Without this, the chat panel explains that it is not
# configured and the rest of SimePark works normally.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Optional. Which Gemini model the assistant calls. If unset, the code default is
# DEFAULT_GEMINI_MODEL in shared/contract/assistant.ts, which is currently:
#     gemini-3.5-flash-lite
#
# Leave this unset to use that default. Model availability, rate limits and
# free-tier eligibility change over time and MUST be checked by the project owner
# in Google AI Studio. This project makes no assumption that any model is
# permanently free. Only set this if you need a specific model your key can use:
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
